1
00:00:00,590 --> 00:00:03,700
I heard from my mom

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:09,590
that you said you want to give me your heart.

3
00:00:09,590 --> 00:00:15,600
What are you trying to get me to do?

4
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:19,150
Kill you so that I can live?

5
00:00:19,150 --> 00:00:22,560
What are you trying to make me do?

6
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:25,750
No. I don't want it.

7
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:28,870
I'd rather die. I don't want it!

8
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:32,170
I came to tell you that.

9
00:00:35,310 --> 00:00:36,800
Why don't you want it?

10
00:00:38,380 --> 00:00:44,190
It's not like I'm dying for you.
I'm going to die regardless.

11
00:00:44,190 --> 00:00:47,920
I want to do something good and end up in heaven.

12
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:50,520
Why? Are you jealous of that as well?

13
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:53,120
Then give it to someone else.

14
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:54,910
Why me?

15
00:00:54,910 --> 00:00:57,310
Why does it have to be me?

16
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:04,250
Because I'm your brother.

17
00:01:05,170 --> 00:01:10,570
You're my little brother, and I'm your big brother.

18
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:12,540
What are you saying?

19
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:16,350
I am your older brother.

20
00:01:16,350 --> 00:01:19,020
I was born from the same mother.

21
00:01:19,020 --> 00:01:23,070
I'm your brother brought into the world
by the same person.

22
00:01:25,740 --> 00:01:28,400
If there's one difference between us,
it's that my twin sister and I

23
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:34,080
were abandoned when we were babies.
As if we were trash.

24
00:01:36,190 --> 00:01:41,160
So stop throwing tantrums and go.

25
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:46,290
I'm too exhausted to tolerate your tantrums.

26
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:59,480
[Episode 14]

27
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:00,650
Mom, that's cheating.

28
00:02:00,650 --> 00:02:01,680
No! You're cheating.

29
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:03,910
- No! Mom, you cheated.
- You cheated.

30
00:02:03,910 --> 00:02:05,780
- I saw it.
- You cheated.

31
00:02:05,780 --> 00:02:07,720
What is this?

32
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:11,840
Rock flinging. You played with me once, remember?

33
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:14,900
Mom! Don't use your whole hand!
You can only use two fingers!

34
00:02:14,900 --> 00:02:17,990
You did it with four fingers a while ago.

35
00:02:17,990 --> 00:02:20,550
Move aside, Seo-kyeong. I'll win for you.

36
00:02:20,550 --> 00:02:22,240
What did you bet? Hot buns?

37
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:23,860
Yeah.

38
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:25,600
Okay! Attack, Kim Galchi.

39
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:27,790
That's so unfair.

40
00:02:27,790 --> 00:02:30,830
Two adults against one child?

41
00:02:30,830 --> 00:02:32,450
My turn.

42
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:43,520
- Hey! It's Choi Yun!.
- What are you doing? I did it.

43
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:45,830
Oh, Choi Yun! Choi Yun! Choi Yun!

44
00:02:45,830 --> 00:02:48,600
- Kim Galchi, it's your turn.
- What did you mean by that?

45
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:58,130
My mom gave birth to you and your sister
and abandoned you?

46
00:02:58,130 --> 00:03:00,590
Are you telling me to believe that?

47
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:06,830
I don't get what you're trying to say right now.

48
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:12,360
Galchi, since we have a guest,
will you go make some tea?

49
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:13,580
Okay.

50
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:16,640
Seo-kyeong, go and help Galchi out.

51
00:03:16,640 --> 00:03:17,790
Okay.

52
00:03:22,650 --> 00:03:24,700
How could that be?

53
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,500
That makes no sense at all.

54
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:37,960
I don't have much time left to live.

55
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:41,960
It's too short a time to even
say things that make sense.

56
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:47,520
If you were me, on the verge of death,
would you talk nonsense?

57
00:03:48,410 --> 00:03:49,830
I don't believe it.

58
00:03:49,830 --> 00:03:51,100
Then don't.

59
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:53,410
Muhyeok.

60
00:03:53,410 --> 00:03:56,080
If you can't believe it, then don't.

61
00:03:57,590 --> 00:04:00,000
Why did you hide it until now?

62
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:03,740
"I'm your child."

63
00:04:03,740 --> 00:04:06,090
"The child that you abandoned."

64
00:04:06,090 --> 00:04:08,570
Why didn't you say that? Why hide it?

65
00:04:11,780 --> 00:04:16,420
Do you know how it feels to get abandoned?

66
00:04:18,450 --> 00:04:23,690
Being abandoned means it's over before it even started.

67
00:04:27,690 --> 00:04:33,190
Even if you were to return, you'd never be welcomed.

68
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:37,650
Being a good son is never showing up at all.

69
00:04:37,650 --> 00:04:39,430
That's what it means.

70
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:48,650
We're not wonderful like you.

71
00:04:48,650 --> 00:04:52,930
One is a worthless gangster wannabe who
doesn't know how long he has left to live,

72
00:04:52,930 --> 00:04:58,680
And the other is too stupid to understand the world.

73
00:04:59,970 --> 00:05:05,970
Even so, we still have pride.
We still feel embarrassment.

74
00:05:07,170 --> 00:05:09,480
I don't believe it.

75
00:05:10,830 --> 00:05:13,010
It doesn't make sense.

76
00:05:14,310 --> 00:05:16,720
You're my mom's son?

77
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:20,150
How can I believe that?

78
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:25,090
I don't believe it! I won't believe it!

79
00:05:25,090 --> 00:05:27,710
If you don't want to believe it, then don't!

80
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:38,890
If you don't want to, then don't.

81
00:05:38,890 --> 00:05:41,570
I will spend the rest of my life

82
00:05:41,570 --> 00:05:45,310
believing that woman is my mother.

83
00:05:45,310 --> 00:05:48,840
It's all I have left to live by.

84
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:55,610
So, if you're embarrassed, why did you return?

85
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:03,350
To get revenge.

86
00:06:05,420 --> 00:06:09,580
I thought it was too unfair to go out that way.
I want revenge.

87
00:06:11,830 --> 00:06:15,640
Oh, before I die I should call her.

88
00:06:18,070 --> 00:06:26,020
Mother, to tell you the truth,
I'm the son you abandoned.

89
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:33,020
And I'm dying. For your oh-so-wonderful son.

90
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:42,380
To save the son you cherish,
your son who is trash will die.

91
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:50,862
For me, would you shed one-millionth of the tears

92
00:06:50,862 --> 00:06:54,470
you shed for Yun, Mother?

93
00:06:55,850 --> 00:06:58,700
I'm leaving.

94
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:53,340
Seo-kyeong.

95
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:55,030
Yes?

96
00:07:55,030 --> 00:07:59,190
That guy is your little brother.

97
00:07:59,190 --> 00:08:00,550
What?

98
00:08:00,550 --> 00:08:05,210
The singer Choi Yun is also your brother.

99
00:08:08,220 --> 00:08:09,840
Galchi, come here.

100
00:08:13,250 --> 00:08:15,380
Between the singer Choi Yun or...

101
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:21,950
I mean... Between Uncle Choi Yun and me,
who's more handsome?

102
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:27,420
Is he cooler or am I?

103
00:08:30,250 --> 00:08:34,030
How come you don't know how to lie?

104
00:08:34,030 --> 00:08:38,020
It's going to be hard for you in the real world
when you grow up, Galchi.

105
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:18,010
Eunchae?

106
00:09:19,830 --> 00:09:21,680
You're Eunchae, right?

107
00:09:23,660 --> 00:09:25,120
Eunchae?

108
00:09:26,190 --> 00:09:27,760
Eunchae?

109
00:09:30,090 --> 00:09:34,140
Galchi? What are you doing here?

110
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:36,550
This is our house.

111
00:09:39,010 --> 00:09:43,110
Let's go in. Uncle and Mom are both home.

112
00:09:45,230 --> 00:09:46,500
Eunchae?

113
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:51,070
Uh... You see.

114
00:09:51,070 --> 00:09:56,130
I was on my way home, but accidentally ended up here.

115
00:09:56,130 --> 00:09:58,910
You weren't coming to our house?

116
00:09:58,910 --> 00:10:03,210
No, I wasn't going to your house.

117
00:10:03,210 --> 00:10:05,600
I wasn't going to your house, Galchi.

118
00:10:06,290 --> 00:10:07,420
Eunchae?

119
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:10,680
I wasn't going to your house.

120
00:10:11,860 --> 00:10:13,440
Sorry.

121
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:17,540
Eunchae...

122
00:10:29,690 --> 00:10:30,990
Hot buns! Hot buns!

123
00:10:30,990 --> 00:10:33,880
Here, Uncle. Have some.

124
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:38,780
Eunchae seems strange, Mom.

125
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:44,710
Did Jjangoo get caught by his mother?

126
00:10:44,710 --> 00:10:45,810
Yeah.

127
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:48,920
Eunchae what?

128
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:50,920
- Did he get beat up a lot?
- Yeah.

129
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:52,820
Eunchae what?

130
00:10:58,320 --> 00:11:00,920
Eunchae what?

131
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:03,650
Eunchae seems a little strange.

132
00:11:03,650 --> 00:11:05,050
Did you see Eunchae?

133
00:11:05,050 --> 00:11:08,880
Yeah. I saw her a while ago in front of our house.

134
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:10,500
Is she in front of the house right now?

135
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:13,630
No, she wasn't coming to our house.

136
00:11:13,630 --> 00:11:16,700
She was going to her house,
but said she accidentally came here.

137
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:31,020
Eunchae? Eunchae?

138
00:11:32,950 --> 00:11:34,270
Eunchae?

139
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:37,300
Eunchae?

140
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:52,710
Sorry!

141
00:11:53,160 --> 00:11:56,490
Blockhead? Are you okay?

142
00:12:25,490 --> 00:12:27,130
Are you okay?

143
00:12:27,130 --> 00:12:28,600
It's cold, huh?

144
00:13:01,570 --> 00:13:04,090
It's so cold.

145
00:13:05,990 --> 00:13:10,830
I wish it was snowing hard right now. That'd be great.

146
00:14:07,270 --> 00:14:08,770
Mister.

147
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:15,030
Mister.

148
00:14:19,860 --> 00:14:21,540
Mister.

149
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:27,660
What are you doing right now?
What are you doing right now?

150
00:14:27,660 --> 00:14:31,180
Why are you looking at the wall
and smiling to yourself so early in the morning?

151
00:14:34,490 --> 00:14:37,980
Here. Yun's mom wanted you to bring the laptop.

152
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:41,540
Oh. Okay.

153
00:15:03,650 --> 00:15:05,170
Blockhead?

154
00:15:10,100 --> 00:15:11,470
Eunchae?

155
00:15:12,540 --> 00:15:14,000
Eunchae?

156
00:15:16,010 --> 00:15:18,090
Blockhead?

157
00:15:18,090 --> 00:15:19,520
Eunchae?

158
00:15:29,030 --> 00:15:32,810
Uncle, what's wrong? What's wrong?

159
00:15:39,780 --> 00:15:44,270
What's wrong? Did you eat too much too quickly?

160
00:15:44,270 --> 00:15:45,510
Yeah.

161
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:49,230
You should have eaten slowly!

162
00:15:49,230 --> 00:15:51,640
Here... Rinse out your mouth.

163
00:15:56,700 --> 00:15:59,110
Did you see Eunchae yesterday?

164
00:16:01,410 --> 00:16:06,260
Did Eunchae really come to our house?

165
00:16:06,260 --> 00:16:07,560
Yes.

166
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:13,360
I couldn't find her.

167
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:15,210
I searched everywhere, but couldn't find her.

168
00:16:15,210 --> 00:16:17,600
Eunchae is dating Choi Yun, right?

169
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:20,400
It said they were going to get married on TV.

170
00:16:32,410 --> 00:16:33,740
Eunchae?

171
00:16:35,190 --> 00:16:36,500
Blockhead?

172
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:26,650
Mister!

173
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:30,090
Mister!

174
00:17:42,070 --> 00:17:44,470
[Heart Disease]
This is too hard.

175
00:17:44,470 --> 00:17:48,150
Why did Mr. Kang bring such difficult books?

176
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:52,030
The font is so small.

177
00:17:52,030 --> 00:17:56,510
Yun, what is heart transplant in English? Huh? Huh?

178
00:17:56,510 --> 00:17:58,910
In English? You don't know?

179
00:18:00,400 --> 00:18:04,230
Huh? Why are you looking at me like that?

180
00:18:04,230 --> 00:18:06,500
Do I have something on my face?

181
00:18:15,050 --> 00:18:17,800
Don't work too hard, Mom.

182
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:18,840
Huh?

183
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:22,900
Don't work too hard to save me.

184
00:18:35,070 --> 00:18:37,380
Yun, is something wrong?

185
00:18:38,770 --> 00:18:44,390
If I'm meant to live, then I'll live somehow.

186
00:18:44,390 --> 00:18:49,320
If I was meant to die, then I'll die somehow.

187
00:18:51,810 --> 00:18:54,490
So don't work so hard, Mom.

188
00:18:54,490 --> 00:18:55,970
Yun.

189
00:18:57,250 --> 00:18:59,960
How can you say something like that
to your own mother?

190
00:19:01,510 --> 00:19:04,660
Is that something a child would dare say to his mother?

191
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:10,370
Is that something to say to your mom?

192
00:19:17,550 --> 00:19:23,230
If it'll save you, I'd do anything.
Anything in my power.

193
00:19:23,230 --> 00:19:26,680
I can do anything. Okay? Fine?

194
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:29,430
If I take Muhyeok's heart and live,

195
00:19:32,530 --> 00:19:34,700
would you be happy?

196
00:19:36,780 --> 00:19:39,910
From now on, don't do anything.

197
00:19:39,910 --> 00:19:41,800
Don't do anything.

198
00:19:44,930 --> 00:19:46,750
I beg you. Please.

199
00:19:49,380 --> 00:19:50,960
Don't do it.

200
00:19:56,010 --> 00:19:57,600
Yun...

201
00:20:18,080 --> 00:20:19,100
Eunchae?

202
00:20:20,110 --> 00:20:21,360
Eunchae?

203
00:20:22,110 --> 00:20:27,160
What are you doing here?
Why aren't you coming inside?

204
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:30,440
Nothing. Nothing.

205
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:34,050
What do you mean nothing?
What's with that expression?

206
00:20:34,050 --> 00:20:35,690
You look insane.

207
00:20:35,690 --> 00:20:38,310
- Eunchae?
- It's nothing.

208
00:20:38,310 --> 00:20:39,740
Eunchae.

209
00:20:39,740 --> 00:20:43,302
♪ Dashing through the snow
In a one-horse open sleigh ♪

210
00:20:43,302 --> 00:20:47,620
- ♪ O'er the fields we go ♪
- ♪ Jingle bells, jingle bells ♪

211
00:20:47,620 --> 00:20:48,770
Seo-kyeong.

212
00:20:50,220 --> 00:20:52,740
- Seo-kyeong.
- Hmm?

213
00:20:52,740 --> 00:20:55,700
Who is Galchi's dad?

214
00:20:57,740 --> 00:20:59,930
Galchi's dad.

215
00:20:59,930 --> 00:21:02,410
Don't you know who Galchi's dad is?

216
00:21:02,410 --> 00:21:03,600
I do know.

217
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:07,700
Where is he right now?

218
00:21:07,700 --> 00:21:08,910
Don't know.

219
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:22,160
Seo-kyeong, you need to meet someone nice and marry.

220
00:21:22,160 --> 00:21:29,300
My sister needs to meet a nice man
and marry before I go.

221
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:37,370
I'm going to marry you, Uncle.

222
00:21:37,370 --> 00:21:39,260
Mom.

223
00:21:39,260 --> 00:21:43,690
Really. I'm going to marry Uncle.

224
00:21:43,690 --> 00:21:45,140
Mom.

225
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:52,100
You cannot marry your own brother.

226
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:53,560
Why not?

227
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:58,290
You can't. You just can't.

228
00:21:58,290 --> 00:22:02,670
I told you that last time.
What is wrong with you?

229
00:22:02,670 --> 00:22:04,810
So frustrating!

230
00:22:04,810 --> 00:22:06,730
Why not?

231
00:22:08,260 --> 00:22:12,130
How can you marry your own brother, you idiot?

232
00:22:12,130 --> 00:22:14,850
What have you spent doing all these years?

233
00:22:14,850 --> 00:22:18,780
Even Galchi knows, but why don't you know?

234
00:22:23,790 --> 00:22:25,880
How long are you going to live like this?

235
00:22:25,880 --> 00:22:27,660
Don't you feel embarrassed in front of Galchi?

236
00:22:27,660 --> 00:22:30,190
Don't you feel sorry?

237
00:22:30,190 --> 00:22:32,450
Listen carefully.

238
00:22:32,450 --> 00:22:37,940
Memorize things you are told
until your head explodes!

239
00:22:40,270 --> 00:22:42,120
Galchi!

240
00:22:42,120 --> 00:22:44,600
Why are you yelling at my mom?

241
00:22:44,600 --> 00:22:46,870
You can just teach her over and over again!

242
00:22:46,870 --> 00:22:51,010
You told me to keep on teaching her
if she doesn't know.

243
00:22:51,010 --> 00:22:54,020
You said that to me,
so why are yelling at my mom?

244
00:22:54,020 --> 00:22:58,300
Why are you yelling at my mom? You're really mean.

245
00:22:59,510 --> 00:23:01,120
Mom, are you okay?

246
00:23:01,120 --> 00:23:04,090
- Here.
- Yes, ma'am.

247
00:23:04,090 --> 00:23:05,440
Lady!

248
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:08,520
Galchi's mom Oh, what's wrong?

249
00:23:08,520 --> 00:23:11,470
What's wrong? Did you cry?

250
00:23:11,470 --> 00:23:14,430
Why are you crying? What's wrong?

251
00:23:14,430 --> 00:23:19,130
What's wrong? What's happening? Huh?

252
00:23:20,270 --> 00:23:25,160
Uncle keeps yelling at me saying I'm stupid.

253
00:23:26,560 --> 00:23:31,050
I don't know what your sister did wrong,

254
00:23:31,050 --> 00:23:33,570
- But one shouldn't do that to their sister, right?
- Yes.

255
00:23:33,570 --> 00:23:35,860
Your sister is sick.

256
00:23:35,860 --> 00:23:38,480
- Take all of it back.
- Mr. Cha.

257
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:40,760
Take all of it back right now!

258
00:23:40,760 --> 00:23:44,790
Mr. Cha. Obviously, there's been
a misunderstanding. The reason I came...

259
00:23:44,790 --> 00:23:50,710
I told you I'd give it to you even
if you don't give me anything.

260
00:23:50,710 --> 00:23:55,640
Even if you don't bring these,
even if you don't beg me,

261
00:23:55,640 --> 00:24:00,400
I've told you already I'm going
to give it to you before I die!

262
00:24:02,080 --> 00:24:06,730
Mr. Cha, seriously. You have me all wrong.

263
00:24:06,730 --> 00:24:08,730
I came here with pure intentions...

264
00:24:08,730 --> 00:24:10,050
Get out.

265
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:12,260
Mr. Cha.

266
00:24:12,260 --> 00:24:14,250
Get out right now.

267
00:24:14,250 --> 00:24:18,090
Take this and get out of my house!

268
00:24:18,090 --> 00:24:19,480
Mr. Cha.

269
00:24:20,390 --> 00:24:22,220
Get out!

270
00:24:24,490 --> 00:24:29,390
You get out! If anyone goes, it should be you!

271
00:24:29,390 --> 00:24:31,680
Why are you yelling at the pretty lady?

272
00:24:31,680 --> 00:24:33,620
You thug.

273
00:24:33,620 --> 00:24:36,740
If anyone goes, it should be you, you dummy.

274
00:24:36,740 --> 00:24:38,060
Mom.

275
00:24:38,680 --> 00:24:40,840
You're so mean?

276
00:24:40,840 --> 00:24:43,400
This is my house, not yours.

277
00:24:43,400 --> 00:24:45,710
If anyone goes, it should be you!

278
00:24:54,290 --> 00:24:55,920
Mr. Cha.

279
00:25:09,370 --> 00:25:13,350
Geez! That stupid jerk.

280
00:25:14,580 --> 00:25:19,550
I wish I could show him how true my intentions are.

281
00:25:22,100 --> 00:25:27,510
I really came here with completely pure intentions.

282
00:25:30,790 --> 00:25:35,820
My Yun. He's been so fussy lately.

283
00:25:35,820 --> 00:25:39,260
And I don't know how to explain it.

284
00:25:39,260 --> 00:25:46,390
But Seo-kyeong and Galchi,
you two keep popping into my head...

285
00:25:49,100 --> 00:25:51,690
You believe me, don't you, Seo-kyeong?

286
00:25:51,690 --> 00:25:52,690
Yes.

287
00:25:53,380 --> 00:25:54,920
Thank you.

288
00:25:56,470 --> 00:25:58,360
Thank you very much.

289
00:25:59,431 --> 00:26:01,718
[Messages from fans:
"Are you okay, Yun?" "Get well soon, Yun]

290
00:26:04,770 --> 00:26:07,790
This is a message from a 40-year-old female fan.

291
00:26:07,790 --> 00:26:09,300
I'll read it.

292
00:26:10,530 --> 00:26:12,460
"Hello, Choi Yun.

293
00:26:12,460 --> 00:26:17,860
I'm a Buddhist monk.
I went to the temple to pray for your health yesterday.

294
00:26:17,860 --> 00:26:20,880
I must have bowed a hundred times to Buddha yesterday.

295
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:23,670
I know it must be tough.

296
00:26:23,670 --> 00:26:26,390
But always remember to have faith and courage."

297
00:26:26,390 --> 00:26:32,960
If I give my heart to Yun, would you come to me?

298
00:26:38,350 --> 00:26:44,050
"Even through hard times,
always love yourself till the end."

299
00:26:44,050 --> 00:26:49,780
If I do one good thing before I die,
maybe I won't go to hell.

300
00:26:49,780 --> 00:26:53,590
And it will be good for you, Yun, and Yun's mom.

301
00:26:55,590 --> 00:26:57,050
Eunchae?

302
00:26:57,860 --> 00:26:59,430
Eunchae?

303
00:27:00,490 --> 00:27:04,260
Yun, I'm going to step out for a while.

304
00:27:04,260 --> 00:27:06,380
One minute.

305
00:27:06,380 --> 00:27:08,490
I'll go out and come back in a minute.

306
00:28:59,260 --> 00:29:00,670
Blockhead?

307
00:29:02,120 --> 00:29:04,020
This is you, isn't it?

308
00:29:06,620 --> 00:29:11,100
Eunchae? This is Eunchae, right?

309
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:16,530
How are you?

310
00:29:17,770 --> 00:29:19,320
You're fine, right?

311
00:29:22,310 --> 00:29:32,710
I'm doing great. I'm really healthy.

312
00:29:35,720 --> 00:29:42,160
You're really okay, right?

313
00:30:35,780 --> 00:30:37,430
Blockhead.

314
00:30:43,750 --> 00:30:45,100
Blockhead.

315
00:30:46,470 --> 00:30:51,660
I missed you so much
I ran all the way here without stopping.

316
00:30:51,660 --> 00:30:53,390
Pretty good, huh?

317
00:30:55,370 --> 00:30:59,490
My little Blockhead,
you're definitely pretty when you smile.

318
00:30:59,490 --> 00:31:04,740
Pretty soon, you'll be prettier than Ms. Australia.

319
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:08,610
Mister.

320
00:31:09,600 --> 00:31:10,900
Eunchae?

321
00:31:11,700 --> 00:31:13,230
Eunchae?

322
00:31:14,990 --> 00:31:16,880
What are you doing?

323
00:31:18,440 --> 00:31:20,870
Who are you smiling at?

324
00:31:23,490 --> 00:31:25,070
Mister?

325
00:31:30,870 --> 00:31:32,660
Mister?

326
00:31:33,550 --> 00:31:35,140
Mister?

327
00:31:35,950 --> 00:31:37,650
Have you gone mad?

328
00:31:38,880 --> 00:31:42,100
Have you finally lost it, Song Eunchae?

329
00:31:42,100 --> 00:31:44,980
Muhyeok is not here.

330
00:31:44,980 --> 00:31:47,420
Where do you see him?

331
00:31:53,770 --> 00:32:00,180
Was it Muhyeok you saw and smiled at just now?

332
00:32:01,350 --> 00:32:02,650
Was it?

333
00:32:04,120 --> 00:32:06,310
No....

334
00:32:06,310 --> 00:32:08,190
No, Yun.

335
00:32:11,770 --> 00:32:13,610
Let's go inside.

336
00:32:15,280 --> 00:32:16,650
Let's go in.

337
00:32:31,860 --> 00:32:33,500
Hey, Sukchae.

338
00:32:35,820 --> 00:32:38,270
Isn't Eunchae a bit strange lately?

339
00:32:40,430 --> 00:32:46,000
Is Eunchae acting a bit weird?
Or saying weird things lately?

340
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:50,550
Eunchae is always strange.

341
00:32:50,550 --> 00:32:53,910
For her to be acting normal is stranger to me.

342
00:32:55,180 --> 00:32:56,350
Give it.

343
00:32:56,350 --> 00:32:58,740
Yun, it's Minchae.

344
00:32:58,740 --> 00:33:01,200
Eunchae was acting weird this morning.

345
00:33:01,200 --> 00:33:05,730
By the gate, as if someone was there,
she was smiling at the wall.

346
00:33:05,730 --> 00:33:08,730
Like crazy people, you know?

347
00:33:08,730 --> 00:33:11,050
- She did that?
- Yup.

348
00:33:13,180 --> 00:33:14,500
Yun?

349
00:33:15,480 --> 00:33:16,670
Yun?

350
00:33:18,500 --> 00:33:19,850
Yun?

351
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:24,360
It's cold. Don't come out.

352
00:34:24,360 --> 00:34:26,960
- No. No.
- It's okay.

353
00:34:26,960 --> 00:34:29,530
Seo-kyeong!
You make the best seaweed rolls in the world!

354
00:34:29,530 --> 00:34:32,100
How do you do it?

355
00:34:32,920 --> 00:34:38,110
You've made me forget all of the
stress I've built up due to Yun.

356
00:34:38,110 --> 00:34:41,160
- I can come back again, right?
- Yeah!

357
00:34:41,160 --> 00:34:44,950
Galchi. Don't be as mean to your mom
as my son's being to me, okay?

358
00:34:44,950 --> 00:34:46,440
Okay.

359
00:34:46,440 --> 00:34:49,210
Parents are the most
vulnerable people in the world.

360
00:34:49,210 --> 00:34:54,070
And I think that people who are bad
to their parents are the worst.

361
00:34:54,070 --> 00:34:55,060
Yeah.

362
00:34:55,060 --> 00:34:57,440
I'm really going. Bye!

363
00:34:58,350 --> 00:35:01,080
- Bye.
- Bye.

364
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:31,050
Eunchae?

365
00:35:34,200 --> 00:35:35,910
Song Eunchae?

366
00:35:55,860 --> 00:35:57,930
Come sit down.

367
00:36:16,590 --> 00:36:22,300
Do you want to go to Muhyeok?

368
00:36:24,210 --> 00:36:28,800
If you want, I'll let go of you.

369
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:36,800
But you can't go to Muhyeok.

370
00:36:40,250 --> 00:36:42,477
Instead of Muhyeok,

371
00:36:45,630 --> 00:36:48,540
tell me when you find someone else.

372
00:36:50,120 --> 00:36:52,620
Then I'll let go.

373
00:36:56,570 --> 00:36:58,610
Ah, I'm sleepy.

374
00:36:59,850 --> 00:37:02,420
I think I should go to sleep.

375
00:37:02,420 --> 00:37:07,690
I feel sleepy all of a sudden.
I won't be able to see you leave.

376
00:37:10,930 --> 00:37:12,120
Bye.

377
00:37:45,850 --> 00:37:47,810
[Choi Yun]

378
00:37:54,630 --> 00:37:57,060
Do you remember what I said?

379
00:37:58,070 --> 00:38:01,960
I said if there is nothing I could do for my woman,

380
00:38:04,100 --> 00:38:06,400
I'd give her up.

381
00:38:07,910 --> 00:38:10,630
I think that is what a man should do.

382
00:38:13,050 --> 00:38:15,330
I called because of Eunchae.

383
00:38:19,450 --> 00:38:21,680
Eunchae is going crazy.

384
00:38:22,480 --> 00:38:28,080
I'm not kidding, seriously. Eunchae is going nuts.

385
00:38:29,190 --> 00:38:30,710
We...

386
00:38:31,630 --> 00:38:34,750
No, you and I have driven her insane.

387
00:38:36,410 --> 00:38:40,020
It was better when we didn't do anything for her.

388
00:38:42,780 --> 00:38:48,140
We are driving Eunchae insane.

389
00:38:49,990 --> 00:38:59,760
I'll let her go. You let her go, too.

390
00:39:01,640 --> 00:39:07,290
The only thing you can give to Eunchae is pain.

391
00:39:10,950 --> 00:39:13,750
Please. Let her go.

392
00:39:19,660 --> 00:39:21,090
No.

393
00:39:45,390 --> 00:39:48,490
Taxi, taxi!

394
00:40:39,060 --> 00:40:40,580
Blockhead.

395
00:40:41,780 --> 00:40:42,670
Eunchae.

396
00:40:42,670 --> 00:40:44,310
Have you gone mad?

397
00:40:44,310 --> 00:40:49,030
Have you finally lost it, Song Eunchae?
Muhyeok is not here.

398
00:40:49,030 --> 00:40:51,300
Where do you see him?

399
00:41:02,260 --> 00:41:06,560
Hey, get out. You call that driving?

400
00:41:06,560 --> 00:41:09,720
Hey, get out! Get out.

401
00:41:09,720 --> 00:41:11,740
Get out while I'm being nice!

402
00:41:12,250 --> 00:41:16,290
Hey! Get out! Get out!

403
00:41:36,440 --> 00:41:37,690
Sorry.

404
00:41:37,690 --> 00:41:41,040
What on earth? It's just a little brat.

405
00:41:41,900 --> 00:41:44,870
Sorry. I'm really sorry.

406
00:41:44,870 --> 00:41:50,120
Girls should just stay home at night.
Why are you out causing trouble?

407
00:41:51,320 --> 00:41:54,430
What? You're staring me down?

408
00:41:54,430 --> 00:41:56,150
What are you looking at?

409
00:41:56,150 --> 00:41:58,630
What are you going to do?

410
00:41:58,630 --> 00:42:00,660
Why I ought to...

411
00:42:01,990 --> 00:42:04,370
Where do you think you're putting your hands?

412
00:42:04,370 --> 00:42:06,800
Should I break your wrists?

413
00:42:23,530 --> 00:42:25,810
It's warm. Drink it.

414
00:42:27,610 --> 00:42:29,260
Drink it.

415
00:42:36,840 --> 00:42:41,260
You're really not going to look at me?

416
00:42:43,330 --> 00:42:45,670
It's because I might wake up.

417
00:42:48,550 --> 00:42:50,900
I might wake up from this dream.

418
00:42:52,410 --> 00:42:54,840
I'm really scared I might wake up.

419
00:42:56,910 --> 00:42:59,200
It's not a dream, Eunchae.

420
00:43:00,230 --> 00:43:02,580
I'm not going to get fooled again.

421
00:43:02,580 --> 00:43:05,770
If I keep fooling myself pretending it's not a dream,

422
00:43:05,770 --> 00:43:08,050
that you're not a dream, then...

423
00:43:09,880 --> 00:43:20,390
That's how I was able to look at you, hold your hands,

424
00:43:20,390 --> 00:43:22,610
and was always fooled.

425
00:43:23,860 --> 00:43:29,010
Then soon someone will say,
"Wake up, Eunchae. It's all a dream."

426
00:43:31,100 --> 00:43:33,160
It's not a dream.

427
00:43:33,160 --> 00:43:38,010
Yun said I've gone nuts.

428
00:43:38,010 --> 00:43:41,240
He said I was going crazy.

429
00:43:42,700 --> 00:43:46,700
I think he's right. I think he's right.

430
00:43:49,720 --> 00:43:51,940
I can't.

431
00:43:53,720 --> 00:43:59,010
Even though I'd rather look at you,

432
00:43:59,010 --> 00:44:02,460
what will I do about my parents?

433
00:44:03,990 --> 00:44:06,560
I can't go crazy.

434
00:44:17,320 --> 00:44:19,060
I'm warm, right?

435
00:44:24,440 --> 00:44:28,240
You feel it beating, don't you?

436
00:44:30,930 --> 00:44:32,910
I'm here.

437
00:44:34,040 --> 00:44:36,400
I'm right beside you.

438
00:45:29,590 --> 00:45:31,940
What is three plus two?

439
00:45:31,940 --> 00:45:33,330
Five.

440
00:45:33,330 --> 00:45:35,500
How about three times eight?

441
00:45:36,580 --> 00:45:38,000
24.

442
00:45:38,610 --> 00:45:42,420
How about 38,824 times 21,365?

443
00:45:43,730 --> 00:45:45,590
How much is that?

444
00:45:46,300 --> 00:45:48,540
I don't know.

445
00:45:48,540 --> 00:45:53,150
Minchae said to check on your mental abilities.

446
00:45:53,150 --> 00:45:55,110
To see if you've lost your marbles or not.

447
00:46:03,730 --> 00:46:05,950
I didn't bring my wallet.

448
00:46:05,950 --> 00:46:07,990
Me, neither.

449
00:46:07,990 --> 00:46:12,970
Sorry. Don't scan these yet.
We forgot to bring our wallets.

450
00:46:13,780 --> 00:46:14,810
Muhyeok!

451
00:46:14,810 --> 00:46:16,340
Hi.

452
00:46:16,340 --> 00:46:19,520
Will you add mine to the pile, too? I'll pay.

453
00:46:19,520 --> 00:46:20,730
Yes, sir.

454
00:46:21,720 --> 00:46:23,030
Muhyeok.

455
00:46:32,460 --> 00:46:34,160
What Dad's name?

456
00:46:34,160 --> 00:46:35,560
Song Daecheon.

457
00:46:35,560 --> 00:46:37,120
Mom's name?

458
00:46:37,120 --> 00:46:38,540
Jang Haesuk.

459
00:46:39,370 --> 00:46:42,910
What does Mom call all 3 of us when she's busy?

460
00:46:42,910 --> 00:46:44,720
I'm fine, Minchae.

461
00:46:44,720 --> 00:46:47,390
What does mom call all three of us?

462
00:46:47,390 --> 00:46:48,590
3 Chaes.

463
00:46:48,590 --> 00:46:51,910
You seem fine. For now. It's cold.

464
00:46:55,550 --> 00:46:58,580
Mister, wear this.

465
00:47:00,370 --> 00:47:01,680
Eunchae.

466
00:47:02,710 --> 00:47:03,970
Let's go.

467
00:47:05,020 --> 00:47:07,800
You're crazy! You're going crazy again!

468
00:47:07,800 --> 00:47:10,600
Why would you take that off? Are you Santa?

469
00:47:10,600 --> 00:47:14,360
He's shaking because he's cold.
I have lots of clothes at home.

470
00:47:14,360 --> 00:47:19,680
Crazy, crazy! Why take it off?

471
00:47:20,760 --> 00:47:24,930
I told you to stay warm. Why won't you listen?

472
00:47:25,720 --> 00:47:29,420
Stay warm, too, Blockhead's sister.

473
00:47:32,510 --> 00:47:35,960
That was really him, right? You saw him too, right?

474
00:47:36,630 --> 00:47:38,050
Yeah.

475
00:47:38,050 --> 00:47:40,980
I understand Sukchae, all of a sudden.

476
00:47:40,980 --> 00:47:42,600
He's definitely hot.

477
00:48:02,310 --> 00:48:03,480
Galchi!

478
00:48:06,600 --> 00:48:10,000
Give your uncle a hot bun, too! It's so cold!

479
00:48:15,320 --> 00:48:17,930
Are you still mad because I yelled at your mom?

480
00:48:19,380 --> 00:48:23,240
It's because I don't have much time.

481
00:48:23,240 --> 00:48:30,230
If I had time, I would teach her 10, 20, or 100 times.

482
00:48:30,230 --> 00:48:34,250
But I don't have the time.

483
00:48:35,550 --> 00:48:41,300
I don't have time to teach her 10 or 100 times.

484
00:48:41,300 --> 00:48:42,840
Why don't you have time?

485
00:48:42,840 --> 00:48:46,150
There are 24 hours in one day.
Why don't you have time?

486
00:48:47,730 --> 00:48:50,860
It's too cold out.

487
00:48:50,860 --> 00:48:53,810
I'm going to turn into an icicle!

488
00:48:53,810 --> 00:48:55,270
I'm going to run home first.

489
00:49:22,100 --> 00:49:23,550
Grandpa.

490
00:49:23,550 --> 00:49:24,790
What?

491
00:49:28,210 --> 00:49:32,410
Why are you wearing the worried
face of a 70-year-old man?

492
00:49:33,390 --> 00:49:35,880
Uncle is a little...

493
00:49:35,880 --> 00:49:37,610
Uncle is what?

494
00:49:37,610 --> 00:49:40,320
Our uncle is going to die, I think.

495
00:49:40,960 --> 00:49:43,080
What are you talking about out of the blue?

496
00:49:43,080 --> 00:49:45,850
Yesterday, when Yun's mom came,
he told her he'd give it to her

497
00:49:45,850 --> 00:49:50,310
before he died, so for her not to
act like she owed him something.

498
00:49:50,310 --> 00:49:51,240
Huh?

499
00:49:51,240 --> 00:49:54,780
And he also said that he didn't
have the time to teach mom

500
00:49:54,780 --> 00:49:59,470
the same thing 10, 100 times.

501
00:50:02,120 --> 00:50:05,710
What's going to happen if Uncle dies, Grandpa?

502
00:50:05,710 --> 00:50:08,960
No way. He won't.

503
00:50:08,960 --> 00:50:14,260
Your uncle is not even 30. He's still really young.
How would he suddenly die?

504
00:50:14,260 --> 00:50:16,630
Don't worry. That won't happen.

505
00:50:32,040 --> 00:50:33,450
Uncle.

506
00:50:33,980 --> 00:50:39,470
Uncle. Wake up. Wake up.

507
00:50:39,470 --> 00:50:44,150
Mom! Mom! Mom, I think Uncle is dead.

508
00:50:44,150 --> 00:50:48,070
Uncle, wake up.

509
00:50:50,960 --> 00:50:54,950
Yun said he won't take it.

510
00:50:54,950 --> 00:50:59,360
He'd rather die and not take Muhyeok's.

511
00:51:01,130 --> 00:51:03,870
Did Yun really like Muhyeok?

512
00:51:05,750 --> 00:51:08,290
Maybe that's why

513
00:51:08,290 --> 00:51:15,110
I can't help but like Muhyeok.

514
00:51:15,110 --> 00:51:18,470
The more I see him, each time we meet.

515
00:51:18,470 --> 00:51:23,400
Muhyeok. His family, too.

516
00:51:24,640 --> 00:51:29,830
As if I've known them for a very long time.

517
00:51:29,830 --> 00:51:32,120
I think it's because I'm old.

518
00:51:33,540 --> 00:51:35,690
I'm going to leave it up to fate.

519
00:51:35,690 --> 00:51:40,710
If something happens to Yun, I'll go, too.

520
00:51:40,710 --> 00:51:42,460
I'll go with him.

521
00:51:50,950 --> 00:51:52,420
What, Galchi?

522
00:51:54,460 --> 00:51:56,090
Uncle what?

523
00:51:57,820 --> 00:52:00,100
Stop crying and tell me.

524
00:52:02,890 --> 00:52:04,900
What happened to your uncle?

525
00:52:05,600 --> 00:52:07,030
Uncle...

526
00:52:07,960 --> 00:52:09,880
Uncle...

527
00:52:10,780 --> 00:52:12,520
What if he doesn't wake up?

528
00:52:12,520 --> 00:52:13,790
Galchi.

529
00:52:13,790 --> 00:52:16,400
- Mom, what are we are going to do?
- Uncle.

530
00:52:20,190 --> 00:52:23,590
[Cha Muhyeok]
- Uncle. / - Uncle, wake up.

531
00:52:36,710 --> 00:52:38,950
Uncle...

532
00:52:38,950 --> 00:52:40,630
Uncle...

533
00:52:42,790 --> 00:52:44,790
What are you going to do?

534
00:52:44,790 --> 00:52:46,490
Uncle!

535
00:52:47,510 --> 00:52:48,890
Eunchae.

536
00:52:48,890 --> 00:52:53,700
He fell down, and we cried...

537
00:53:02,780 --> 00:53:05,000
Muhyeok fainted.

538
00:53:11,660 --> 00:53:14,130
He's in bad shape.

539
00:53:14,130 --> 00:53:19,700
The doctors say he might not make
it past the next couple weeks.

540
00:53:30,120 --> 00:53:31,780
Are you scared?

541
00:53:32,980 --> 00:53:37,550
I got shot at my wife's wedding.

542
00:53:37,550 --> 00:53:42,100
The bullet was lodged in a place
too dangerous to remove.

543
00:53:42,100 --> 00:53:48,400
The bullet is right here.

544
00:53:50,090 --> 00:53:51,400
Scary, huh?

545
00:53:58,020 --> 00:54:07,990
Will you look after Seo-kyeong and Galchi

546
00:54:09,680 --> 00:54:14,210
later when I'm gone?

547
00:55:24,560 --> 00:55:27,140
Eunchae is going nuts.

548
00:55:27,140 --> 00:55:29,190
We...

549
00:55:29,190 --> 00:55:32,330
No, you and I have driven her insane.

550
00:55:32,330 --> 00:55:35,750
It was better when we didn't do anything for her.

551
00:55:36,610 --> 00:55:44,270
There was so much I wanted to give you.
But I've only given you pain.

552
00:55:49,540 --> 00:55:53,780
I have nothing to give but that.

553
00:55:55,470 --> 00:56:00,000
The only thing you can give to Eunchae is pain.

554
00:56:01,210 --> 00:56:03,770
Let her go.

555
00:57:22,297 --> 00:57:25,262
[Cha Muhyeok]

556
00:57:30,650 --> 00:57:34,400
I'm shocked you're calling me.
What's going on?

557
00:58:06,630 --> 00:58:08,030
Mister.

558
00:58:20,590 --> 00:58:24,100
What's wrong? What happened? What happened, Muhyeok?

559
00:58:27,720 --> 00:58:30,890
Take me somewhere.

560
00:58:30,890 --> 00:58:32,810
In your condition? Where could I take you?

561
00:58:32,810 --> 00:58:35,040
You can't go anywhere like this.

562
00:58:35,040 --> 00:58:36,500
Anywhere.

563
00:58:37,680 --> 00:58:42,510
Somewhere far from Seoul.

564
00:58:42,510 --> 00:58:46,820
Take me somewhere far from here.

565
00:58:49,310 --> 00:58:53,050
Take me.

566
00:58:53,050 --> 00:58:54,650
Please.

567
00:59:10,170 --> 00:59:11,730
Mister.

568
00:59:13,690 --> 00:59:15,290
Mister.

569
00:59:17,350 --> 00:59:18,970
Mister.

570
00:59:19,740 --> 00:59:21,510
Mister.

571
00:59:35,158 --> 00:59:41,051
I'm your son too!

572
00:59:42,532 --> 00:59:52,683
You gave birth to me just like you did Yun!

573
00:59:52,758 --> 00:59:56,180
I'm your blood too!

574
01:00:09,386 --> 01:00:14,268
Let me just see your face before I go.

575
01:00:14,268 --> 01:00:17,916
I'll just see your face before I leave.

576
01:00:20,748 --> 01:00:23,716
I said don't talk about him!
